    "body": "The main motivating example is this from the [CompressionStream explainer](https://github.com/ricea/compressstream-explainer/blob/master/README.md#example-code):\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nasync function compressArrayBuffer(in) {\r\n  const cs = new CompressionStream('deflate');\r\n  const writer = cs.writable.getWriter();\r\n  writer.write(in);\r\n  writer.close();\r\n  const out = [];\r\n  const reader = cs.readable.getReader();\r\n  let totalSize = 0;\r\n  while (true) {\r\n    const { value, done } = await reader.read();\r\n    if (done)\r\n      break;\r\n    out.push(value);\r\n    totalSize += value.byteLength;\r\n  }\r\n  const concatenated = new Uint8Array(totalSize);\r\n  let offset = 0;\r\n  for (const array of out) {\r\n    concatenated.set(array, offset);\r\n    offset += array.byteLength;\r\n  }\r\n  return concatenated;\r\n}\r\n```\r\nwhere it took 3 lines just to create a stream containing a single ArrayBuffer chunk, something that feels like it should be a one-liner. This is also a possible solution to https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/809.\r\n\r\n*Edit:*\r\n\r\nBy \"three lines\" I meant turning\r\n```javascript\r\n  const writer = cs.writable.getWriter();\r\n  writer.write(in);\r\n  writer.close();\r\n```\r\ninto\r\n```javascript\r\n  ReadableStream.from(in).pipeTo(cs.writable);\r\n```",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
