    "created_at": "2020-02-18T09:29:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-18T09:29:47Z",
    "body": "> It would behave the same as `Array.from(uint8array)`. Perhaps we should add `ReadableStream.of(...chunks)` to mirror `Array.of(...elements)`?\r\n\r\nI prefer this to making `rs.from(uint8array)` a special-case. If we special case buffer source types, then we also have to special case strings. Strings are arguably worse, since if you `rs.from('word')` then you get a stream of 4 1-character strings, which will appear to work but perform horribly.\r\n\r\nIs there a way to express `of(...)` in WebIDL?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
